Free for any use

What this is. The contents of this directory are the compatibility profile
database: knowledge of the settings particular programs need.

1. Permission

Anyone may use, copy, modify, combine, distribute, sell and include these
contents in their own products, commercial ones included. Without conditions,
without attribution, without asking and free of charge. This permission is
perpetual, worldwide and irrevocable.

2. Waiver

The rights holder waives all rights in these contents to the fullest extent
permitted by applicable law — including copyright, database rights in the
compilation, and any neighbouring rights.

3. If the waiver does not take effect

The law of some countries does not allow copyright to be waived. Wherever the
waiver in section 2 is wholly or partly ineffective, section 1 applies: an
unconditional, perpetual, worldwide and irrevocable permission. Section 1 is the
operative grant; section 2 only strengthens it where that is possible.

4. Contributions

By sending a profile here, a person agrees to all of the above in respect of
what they send. They retain no rights over it and receive nothing from us.

5. No warranty

These contents are provided as is. Nobody warrants that they are correct,
applicable, or that they will lead to anything. Use them at your own risk.

Why. This is not software but collected observations. Knowing that a game needs
a particular setting is obtained by spending an evening on that game, and
keeping it as property would only make the next person spend the same evening.
